  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The measures of the interior angles of a convex polygon of \\(n\\) sides are in arithmetic progression. If the common difference is \\(5^\\circ\\) and the largest angle is \\(160^\\circ,\\) then \\(n\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(16\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(32\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "9"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The smallest angle is \\(160-5(n-1).\\) The angle sum is \\(\\frac n2\\) times \\(320-5(n-1),\\) and it equals \\(180(n-2).\\) This simplifies to \\[ \\begin{aligned} n^2+7n-144&=0,\\\\ (n-9)(n+16)&=0. \\end{aligned} \\] Thus \\(n=9.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the smallest angle as \\(160-5(n-1)\\)",
        "Equate the arithmetic-series sum to \\(180(n-2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
